        "content": "<p>When I typed the following, I got an error: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there no instance of this form in mathlib?</p>\n<p>I assume not, and so I tried constructing my own (in my own code) and ran into some problem I don't entirely understand. The following is what I typed:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SMul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">smul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>And, I got the following error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>cannot find synthesization order for instance @«instSMulOfModuleOfAlgebra_external:file:///MathlibDemo/MathlibDemo.lean» with type\n  {R S M : Type} →\n    [inst : CommRing R] → [inst_1 : CommRing S] → [inst_2 : AddCommGroup M] → [Module S M] → [Algebra R S] → SMul R M\nall remaining arguments have metavariables:\n  CommRing ?S\n  @Module ?S M CommRing.toCommSemiring.toSemiring inst✝².toAddCommMonoid\n  @Algebra R ?S CommRing.toCommSemiring CommRing.toCommSemiring.toSemiring\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I am confused as to why this did not work. Could someone please help me out?</p>",
        "id": 617475670,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1787152219
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can read the docstring of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RestrictScalars#doc\">docs#RestrictScalars</a>: usually, what you want to do is to put an extra <code>Module R M</code> instance as a parameter and pair it with an <code>IsScalarTower R S M</code> instance.</p>",
        "id": 617477664,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1787152758
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you need this instance to <em>state</em> a theorem or or to make a definition, what you would do is add a <code>[Module R M] [IsScalarTower R S M]</code> assumption. If you need this instance internal to a proof (but it doesn't show up in the statement) you can use <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RestrictScalars#doc\">docs#RestrictScalars</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Module.restrictScalars#doc\">docs#Module.restrictScalars</a>.</p>",
        "id": 617478380,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787152932
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"286014\">@Robin Carlier</span> and <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"816344\">@Aaron Liu</span>  thanks a lot. This is really helpful. But, even after reading the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=RestrictScalars#doc\">docs#RestrictScalars</a>, I do not understand why this is done like this rather than just creating an instance?</p>\n<p>Additionally, why do I get an error when I try creating that instance myself?</p>",
        "id": 617478920,
        "sender_full_name": "Abhijit A J",
        "timestamp": 1787153085
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The issue is that typeclass search only knows about the type <code>Module R M</code> when searching for an instance, so it cannot guess that there is some <code>S</code> and some <code>Algebra R S</code> such that <code>Module S M</code>. The error you are having when adding this instance is essentially telling you that <code>S</code> cannot be guessed from the return type <code>Module R M</code> alone.</p>",
        "id": 617479367,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1787153206
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, okay. I get it. Thank you!</p>",
